DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssiiggrreettuurrnn() system call allows users to atomically unmask, switch
     stacks, and return from a signal context.  The thread's signal mask and
     stack status are restored from the context structure pointed to by _s_c_p.
     The system call does not return; the users stack pointer, frame pointer,
     argument pointer, and processor status longword are restored from the
     context.  Execution resumes at the specified pc.  This system call is
     used by the trampoline code and longjmp(3) when returning from a signal
     to the previously executing program.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, the system call does not return.  Otherwise, a value of -1
     is returned and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The ssiiggrreettuurrnn() system call will fail and the thread context will remain
     unchanged if one of the following occurs.

     [EFAULT]           The _s_c_p argument points to memory that is not a valid
                        part of the process address space.

     [EINVAL]           The process status longword is invalid or would im‐
                        properly raise the privilege level of the process.

